Description: Let the server show one window to its own screen shooter
 Umoja shows live window thumbnails (Alt+Tab, overview, dock menu), and Mir
 can only capture an area of the screen with everything on it. If the
 server executable exports a C function named mir_scene_filter_hook, the
 surface stack asks it about every surface (and once with a null surface
 for the overlays) when building a compositor's scene: 1 shows the
 surface even when it is hidden (minimized, on another workspace), 0
 leaves it out, -1 keeps the usual rules. umoja-mir answers only for a
 screen shooter it created itself, so outputs and screencopy clients are
 unaffected. Without the hook nothing changes; no ABI change.
Author: Umoja developers
Forwarded: no

--- a/src/server/scene/surface_stack.cpp	2026-11-13 01:33:00.748849558 +0000
+++ b/src/server/scene/surface_stack.cpp	2026-11-13 01:33:00.750465587 +0000
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #include <mir/log.h>
 
 #include <boost/throw_exception.hpp>
+#include <dlfcn.h>
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <functional>
@@ -147,16 +148,37 @@
     }
